# Copy to .env.local and fill in values from your Supabase project
# (Project Settings → API). Never put the service_role key in the frontend.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Setup checklist:
# 1. Create a free project at https://supabase.com
# 2. Run supabase/schema.sql in the SQL editor (re-run it if the table already exists)
# 3. Auth → URL Configuration:
#    Site URL = http://localhost:5173
#    Redirect URLs = http://localhost:5173/**
# 4. Google Cloud → OAuth client (Web application):
#    JavaScript origin: http://localhost:5173
#    Authorized redirect URI: https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#    While the consent screen is in Testing, add your Google account as a test user.
# 5. Auth → Providers → Google: paste that client ID and secret.
#    If Google returns a nonce error, turn on "Skip nonce check".
# 6. Optional for local dev: Auth → Providers → Email → turn off "Confirm email"
